==English==
{{wikipedia|mul=allophone (Canada)}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|allo-|gloss1=different|-phone}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈaləˌfəʊn/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæləˌfoʊn/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-allophone.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæləˌfəʉn/|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|phonology}} Any of two or more alternative pronunciations for a [[phoneme]].
#: {{ux|en|In some languages, [ʋ] is an '''allophone''' of /v/.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Mikhail Sergeevich Andronov|title=A Comparative Grammar of the Dravidian Languages|publisher=Otto Harrassowitz Verlag|isbn=9783447044554|page=33
|passage=In the former the bilabial phone forms an '''allophone''' of the phoneme /v/ in word-final position after /a/ and an '''allophone''' of the phoneme /u/ when it is preceded by an obstruent and followed by /a/; {{...}}}}
# A person whose [[mother tongue]] is one other than that spoken by the majority.
## {{lb|en|Quebec}} A person whose [[mother tongue]] is neither English, French, nor (sometimes) an indigenous language.

