===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|Canada}} Of or relating to those whose mother tongue is neither English, French, nor (sometimes) an indigenous language of Canada.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Charles Boberg|title=The English Language in Canada: Status, History and Comparative Analysis|publisher=Cambridge University Press|isbn=9781139491440|page=23
|passage=In every case the '''allophone''' population is vastly larger than the proportion of francophones, which ranges from 4.2 percent {{...}} from other parts of Canada more than international immigration from abroad: despite a growing '''allophone''' presence, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Statistics Canada|title=Canada Year|isbn=9780660199597
|passage=As immigration increases from different parts of the world, the  linguistic makeup of Canada changes. In 2006, the '''allophone''' population—individuals whose mother tongue is neither English nor French—totalled 6.3  million, {{...}}}}
# That which is of a language other than that spoken by the majority.

